is get_once_registry."] [179 1 "// defaultActionOf is get_default_action."] [195 1 "// warnMatched is check_matched: None matches, an exact str must be equal, else the filter's match(arg) decides."] [214 1 "// filterSearch is filter_search: the first matching filter's action and the filter, or nil."] [254 1 "// getFilter is get_filter: the context's filters when a context is set, else the global ones, else the default action."] [279 1 "// alreadyWarned is already_warned: the registry cleared when its version is not the filters', then key's entry."] [316 1 "// normalizeModule is normalize_module: the file name less a \".py\" suffix, \"<unknown>\" for an empty one."] [328 1 "// showWarningFallback is show_warning: \"file:line: Category: text\" and the source line on sys.stderr, errors ignored."] [349 3 "// _Py_DisplaySourceLine opens the file by its name: a \"<string>\" or \"<stdin>\" has no lines to show"] [357 1 "// warnStrText is str(o)'s text, \"\" when it fails."] [366 1 "// callShowWarning is call_show_warning: warnings._showwarnmsg(WarningMessage(...)), else the fallback."] [400 1 "// warnExplicit is warn_explicit, the lock held by the caller."] [519 1 "// warnInternalFilename is is_internal_filename: importlib's bootstrap."] [537 1 "// warnFrames is the thread's Python frames, the innermost first."] [545 1 "// setupContext is setup_context: the frame stacklevel up (importlib's bootstrap frames and those of the skipped file"] [546 1 "// prefixes not counted once the first frame is not one), its file name, line, __name__ and __warningregistry__"] [547 1 "// (made when absent); \"<sys>\", 0 and sys's globals when there is no such frame."] [587 1 "// warnCategory is get_category."] [605 1 "// warningsWarn is do_warn under the lock."] [625 1 "// warnSourceLine is get_source_line: the module's loader's get_source(name), its line lineno, or nil."] [678 1 "// blessMyLoader is _PyImport_BlessMyLoader: importlib._bootstrap_external._bless_my_loader(module_globals), the"